@node ``goldendict-ng not found''
@section ``goldendict-ng not found''

This error means @code{executable-find} cannot locate the binary specified in @code{goldendict-ng-executable} (@ref{Executable path}). Verify that GoldenDict-NG is installed and set the user option to the full path of the executable.

@node ``Language detection requires GNU Aspell''
@section ``Language detection requires GNU Aspell''

This error appears when @code{goldendict-ng-narrow-groups-to-matching-languages} is non-nil but Aspell is not installed (@ref{Language detection}). Install Aspell and the relevant language dictionaries for your configured groups.

@node ``Zero candidates''
@section ``Zero candidates''

This error means that, after language-based filtering, no dictionary groups match the search string, and @code{goldendict-ng-show-all-group} is @code{nil} (@ref{@code{goldendict-ng-show-all-group}}). Either set @code{goldendict-ng-show-all-group} to @code{t} so the ``All'' group is always available as a fallback, or add more language groups to your configuration.

